  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Restoring Fisheries for Sustainable Livelihoods in Lake Malawi (REFRESH)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Malawi):  USAID&apos;s REFRESH activity addresses priority threats to biodiversity while diversifying livelihoods to reduce climate risk for healthy ecosystems and increased climate resilience for Malawians e involved in the fisheries industry. Covering all eight of the districts bordering Lake Malawi, REFRESH in its second year of implementation will: (1) build capacity among communities and districts to form and/or strengthen local fisheries management authorities to develop and implement local fisheries plans, link to district councils, increase revenue, and support enforcement; (2) support the National Fisheries Research Unit to conduct total catch and fishing intensity assessments, which support commercial and artisanal fisheries with scientifically sound management regimes; (3) train the Fisheries Enforcement Unit to combat and successfully prosecute illegal, unregulated, and unreported fishing crimes in Lake Malawi; (4) scale up conservation enterprises to help reduce pressure on wild caught fisheries; and, (5) build constituencies for effective, accountable, and transparent ecosystem-based fisheries management. .By 2024, REFRESH will result in: (1) the establishment of 1,500,000 hectares of biologically significant area for improved natural resource management that include fish sanctuaries and estuaries identified in the International Union for Conservation of Nature&apos;s Key Biodiversity Areas for Lake Malawi. In addition, REFRESH will result in a stronger and more sustainable fisheries sector  - the country&apos;s main source of protein and critical for nutrition; build citizen capacity at district level, with strengthened Beach Village Committees and District Councils; support conservation enterprises; and establish sustainable financing mechanisms. .This activity will support the Mission&apos;s ICS  Objective 2.3 - Nurture entrepreneurship, unleashing the ingenuity of the Malawian people to self-realize a better economic future..</narrative>
  </description>
